From bc4aca4b14387d6443fa1e817f5a73aaa9d9fcb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:23:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: bug 22: merge the copies of a wildcard arm into
 one dispatch region

The pattern compiler gives a match on an enum one subtree per variant
(semi/pattern.rs, `Family::Variant`), so a wildcard arm is copied into
every variant it covers, and codegen emits one single-tag
`reussir.record.dispatch` region per copy (codegen lower/expr.rs,
`ctor_switch`). Each copy releases the values the arm holds; the
decrement expansion and the first acquire/drop expansion then expand
each release of a value of unknown variant in line as a match over all
its variants. A derived equality over N constructors (an outer match on
`a` whose arm i matches `b` against constructor i, with `_ => ...`) thus
becomes N arms x (N - 1) copies x an N-way release: N^3 code. A derived
BEq on 40 constructors took 9 minutes to build.

The dispatch op already has regions over several tags. Add a
canonicalization to `reussir.record.dispatch`: regions that do not use
their payload argument and hold the same operations (attributes and
locations included, on the same values from outside; candidates grouped
by a structural hash first) become one region over the union of their
tags, without the argument. Running the same code for every merged tag
is what the copies did, so the program is unchanged. The canonicalizer
runs in the inliner and after the first SCCP, before the decrement
expansion, so each wildcard arm is expanded once. Passes that need the
variant of a region (destructuring decrement fusion, variant tag
inference) already skip regions over several tags; the release of the
scrutinee there is a plain decrement (its drop dispatches on the tag, and
its token is a dynamic one that token reuse can still realloc).

Repro reussir-bugs/repros/bug22-wildcard-wide-enum.py (rrc -O aggressive,
to an executable, this machine under load): N = 10: 1.7 s -> 0.6 s;
N = 20: 15.0 s -> 1.8 s; N = 30: 136 s -> 3.7 s; N = 40: 444 s (before,
from the entry) -> 7.8 s. Same output (100).

A region that boxes a value of the scrutinee's own type is not merged:
in its per-tag copies the release of the scrutinee is a decrement of that
tag's cell, which the construction reuses in place when the sizes match,
while a merged region's release has a cell of unknown size, reused through
a reallocation (`_ => E::b{k, k, k}`: reuse decisions {ensure 1, realloc
2, allocate 2} became {realloc 1}; found by the adversarial review,
RV8C-03).

Smaller functions also reach the inliner's size cap sooner: on lean2rr's
StateT tower built without its inlining workaround (bug 20), rrc's peak
memory went from 1.8 GB to 2.4 GB with this commit alone; bug 20's commit
brings the series to 1.0 GB. With the workaround: unchanged.

Tests: tests/integration/conversion/record_dispatch_merge.mlir (the merge,
what is kept apart, and an executable check that the merged dispatch runs
the right code for every tag), record_dispatch_merge_boxing.mlir (regions
boxing the dispatched type stay apart).
